"Implemented (commit d337ead) per user's account-ingestion design. roles (seeded 'admin' at init) + account_roles relation; require_admin resolves identity -> account -> role AND refuses accounts flagged requires_password_rotation. push_assets admin-gated. Token lifecycle: scripts/publish.sh (now the po publish command) takes TRPG_ADMIN_TOKEN from env, publishes, immediately calls bootstrap_admin -> creates 'admin' account (no player), grants role, stores salted sha256 hash in PRIVATE account_passwords, flags rotation. Claim via login_with_password (only usable on accounts with ZERO attached identities -- passwords can never silently attach to a held account, preserving the confirmed-login guarantee); set_password overwrites the hash and clears the flag: the token is eliminated at claim+rotation. Plaintext exists only in the publish action's env + the single reducer call; never in git or tables. UI reuses account models: password login inputs on the account screen, a blocking rotation screen, an admin-only push-assets control. E2E phase 1 walks the ladder (unattached push refused / bootstrap once-only / wrong token / unrotated push refused / rotation unlocks / old token dead); all pushing phases seed via a claimed admin. Notes: sha256+salt is interim (argon2 heavy in wasm; revisit before real exposure); bootstrap_admin has an accepted publish-to-bootstrap first-caller race (back-to-back in one action on a wiped DB); po publish now requires TRPG_ADMIN_TOKEN in env."